#!clock=5
# The Enchanted Glade (v550): full win in 137 steps (`#!clock=5` for the dryad's 15 s + 10 s arrow timers). The quest is to sprinkle the temple's sacred water on the silver birch in the enchanted glade, freeing the Lady of the Woods.
# Inn: torch under the bed (switch it on - the mine's dead end kills you in the dark); the cup/coffee pot must stay behind (leaving with either bounces you back), canopener and biscuit -> eat biscuit = crumbs. Trolley from the beach linked to the others in the village exposes a pound coin in the handle (`x handle`); coin to the ice-cream man, eat the lolly, drop the stick in the litter bin, `feel in litter bin` -> bottle.
# Grotto: `watch lizard` (instead of waiting 5 s) shows the lever, `pull lever`, `enter`; sea cave `climb wall`, `x nest` reveals the small key, which opens the iron door to the library (cupboard whistle). Crystal forest: `throw crumbs` -> tiny gold acorn. Blow the whistle at the sea-cave entrance, `climb dolphin` to the beach, give the acorn to the dryad at once (the arrow clock starts when you enter the forest edge).
# Mine: pull the tin-mine ring, down, east; up on the moor take the toad from the boggy place (`x grass`), drop it in the cobwebby tunnel (spiders), torch on in the dead end, `use canopener on tin`, `x tin`, eat the spinach (strong). Tor summit `push rock`, `take large key` (two keys). Temple: `open oak door`, `turn stone` then menu 3 (the wriggly line; the other two stones are adders), `fill bottle`, then `sprinkle water` in the glade.
